  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FPP Forest dependent people benefit from REDD</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">FPP Skogsfolk tj&#xe4;nar p&#xe5; REDD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Minskade utsl&#xe4;pp fr&#xe5;n minskad avskogning och skogsdegradering (REDD)  &#xe4;r  den huvudinriktningen p&#xe5; skogslandet DRKs klimatarbete. Den stora fr&#xe5;gan &#xe4;r dock hur medel ska n&#xe5; fram till lokalbefolkningen som i     m&#xe5;nga fall inte ens vet vad de har f&#xf6;r r&#xe4;ttigheter. Detta projekt     syftar till att st&#xe4;rka deras kompetens om just detta genom den        internationella NGOn Forest Peoples Programme.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduced emissions from deforestation and forest degradation (REDD) is the main focus for DRC&apos;s (second largest rain forest in the world)    climate change work. The big question is how local people will        benefit from the scheme when, in many cases, the don&apos;t even know      their rights. This project together with Forest Peoples Programme     aims to strengthen their capacity on this subject.</narrative>
  </description>
